 "researcher_notes": "The Michigan Public Service Commission news release of May 15, 2025 says it approved a certificate of public convenience and necessity for SEMCO Energy Gas Company to build the Keweenaw Connector Pipeline, case U-21780. It is a 30-mile, 12-inch steel gas transmission line between Three Lakes and Baraga in Baraga County. A local TV6 news story of May 16, 2025 repeats the same facts and is not an independent source. Length of 30 miles (about 48 km) meets the 25 km rule. This is not the Marquette Connector (P0313, Arnold to Negaunee) or the Risberg Line; no existing row covers Baraga County. Status is proposed because the certificate is granted but no construction start was found. Capacity, cost, in-service date and route geometry were not found in these sources. Owner spelled as the ownership gazetteer has it (SEMCO Energy); the order names SEMCO Energy Gas Company. Route: none available, no official GIS found."
